      "games/rust/README.md (What works, what doesn't — compile proof on Carbon 2.0.259 / build 25454815; protocol harness last run on build 25353106, no client)"
    ],
    "notes": "Rust Dedicated Server public build 25454815 (2026-09-22) with Carbon production build v2.0.259 (protocol 2026.09.03.0, commit 21063e8, GitHub release asset id 547241271). The current plugin compiles against this exact pair; load, identify, reachability, catalogues, console, broadcast, reconnect and shutdown were last proven by takaro-maint verify on build 25353106 with the same Carbon bytes and no client. Player hooks and gameplay are not proven. Carbon's production_build tag is re-uploaded in place, so what pins these bytes is the recorded sha256/size, not the tag. Carbon publishes no machine-readable Rust-build compatibility, so a new Rust head is filed blocked-upstream until a target pinning a compatible Carbon lands. Runtime CI is #167; gameplay evidence #174."
  },
